  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shambhu Singh vs The State Of Bihar on 12 March, 2013",
    "facts": "The Petitioner seeks bail in a case instituted for the offence under Sections 26(i)(iv), 31, 42, 48 and 50 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, Sections 2, 3 and 4 of the Exchange Act.",
    "arguments": "(ii) That the affidavit shall clearly state that the Petitioner is not an accused in any other case and if he is, he shall not be released on bail. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that he has been implicated repeatedly at the instance of the local police, who is hostile to the petitioner, and seeks protection of a person well reputed doing social service in the area.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that he has been implicated repeatedly at the instance of the local police, who is hostile to the petitioner, and seeks protection of a person well reputed doing social service in the area.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "(ii) That the affidavit shall clearly state that the Petitioner is not an accused in any other case and if he is, he shall not be released on bail."
